<fieldset class="min-w-0 space-y-3">
  <legend class="block text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Kobo Store on this reader</legend>
  <label class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-4 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:border-blue-500 has-[:checked]:bg-blue-950/30">
    <%= form.radio_button :store_coexistence, true, class: "mt-1 shrink-0 border-gray-600 bg-gray-800 text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-gray-900", aria: { describedby: "kobo-mode-store-help" } %>
    <span class="min-w-0">
      <span class="block font-medium text-white">Keep my Kobo Store library <span class="ml-1 rounded bg-blue-900/60 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-normal text-blue-200">Recommended</span></span>
      <span id="kobo-mode-store-help" class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-400">Shelfarr books appear beside your purchases. The reader stays signed in to its own Kobo account: Shelfarr passes Store requests to Kobo and never saves that sign-in. Needs an HTTPS address.</span>
    </span>
  </label>
  <label class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-4 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:border-blue-500 has-[:checked]:bg-blue-950/30">
    <%= form.radio_button :store_coexistence, false, class: "mt-1 shrink-0 border-gray-600 bg-gray-800 text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-gray-900", aria: { describedby: "kobo-mode-local-help" } %>
    <span class="min-w-0">
      <span class="block font-medium text-white">Shelfarr books only</span>
      <span id="kobo-mode-local-help" class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-400">Replaces Store syncing. Store books already on the reader stay, but new purchases and Store reading places wait until you restore the original endpoint.</span>
    </span>
  </label>
</fieldset>
<fieldset class="min-w-0 space-y-3">
  <legend class="block text-sm text-gray-300 mb-2">Reading places</legend>
  <label class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-4 cursor-pointer">
    <%= form.check_box :share_progress, class: "mt-1 shrink-0 rounded border-gray-600 bg-gray-800 text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-gray-900", aria: { describedby: "kobo-share-help" } %>
    <span class="min-w-0">
      <span class="block font-medium text-white">Share reading places with Shelfarr</span>
      <span id="kobo-share-help" class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-400">From this Kobo to Shelfarr. When you read a Shelfarr book on this Kobo, the web and mobile readers resume there, if it is the same edition and the most recent place. Kobo places are shared by chapter and percentage, so the exact page can differ. Places that can't be compared automatically wait here for you to choose.</span>
    </span>
  </label>
  <label class="flex gap-3 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-gray-800/60 p-4 cursor-pointer">
    <%= form.check_box :receive_progress, class: "mt-1 shrink-0 rounded border-gray-600 bg-gray-800 text-blue-600 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-gray-900", aria: { describedby: "kobo-receive-help" } %>
    <span class="min-w-0">
      <span class="block font-medium text-white">Receive Shelfarr reading places <span class="ml-1 rounded bg-amber-900/60 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-normal text-amber-200">Preview</span></span>
      <span id="kobo-receive-help" class="mt-1 block text-sm text-gray-400">From Shelfarr to this Kobo. After you read in the web reader or the Android or iOS app, this Kobo opens the book there at its next Wi-Fi sync. Books sent from your library can receive places: EPUB files are sent as a Kobo edition (KEPUB) that Shelfarr prepares from the original, which stays unchanged, and KEPUB files are sent as they are. Kobo opens the same chapter at the nearest sentence marker, so the page can differ slightly. Plain EPUB files sent before Kobo editions (until you send them again), books shared from Kobo accounts and Kobo Store books keep their Kobo place, and a newer place on this Kobo is never replaced. Not yet tested on a physical Kobo.</span>
    </span>
  </label>
</fieldset>
